<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Telecom down 2.51 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Telecom down 2.51 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan Telecommunications Company Ltd (PTCL) fell 0.65 rupees, or 2.51 percent, to 25.25 on Monday on selling of its Global Depositary Receipts (GDR) abroad, dealers said.</p>
<p>A turnover of 300,000 shares of PTCL had been recorded at the Karachi stock exchange by midsession.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been some heavy conversion of PTCL GDRs in the local market, which depressed its price,&quot; dealer Sohaib Latif of KASB &amp; Co said. &quot;But we might see a rally in PTCL in the near term as there are rumours of an increase in line rent.&quot;</p>
<p>PTCL officials could not immediately be reached for comment.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192.</p>
